{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"pr-1909-code-weight-loss-audit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"PR #1909 code-weight loss audit"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Frozen reduction: Retire internal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Scheduler.onClear"},{"type":"text","value":" notifications and pending-aware dependency objects because production has no callers. Dependencies then wait only for queued jobs. Replace synthetic tests with queued-job cancellation, exact failure identity, and recovery checks. Remove Effect's retained "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pipeline"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tracksPublishedRows"},{"type":"text","value":" fields because the first is used once and the second duplicates the ordered-loader map. Remove unused "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduleGraphRun"},{"type":"text","value":" job ID and dependency overrides."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The before source is commit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"80421c8b"},{"type":"text","value":". The after source is code commit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"b69c189c"},{"type":"text","value":". Two agents scanned the source versions separately after reading the field-lab loss-audit card and live-query architecture. The entries below are source-supported omissions from the frozen reduction. They do not decide whether to restore an item or whether a behavior regressed."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recovered distinction and pointer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where dropped"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A dependency could block through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasPendingGraphRun(contextId)"},{"type":"text","value":" even without a queued job. Otherwise an absent dependency was satisfied ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"80421c8b:scheduler.ts:126-144"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queued-only clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit rejection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rescheduling replaced a callback without moving its queue position; omitted dependencies retained the prior set. A running job left the map before reentrant work ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.ts:84-101,147-152"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancellation clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear()"},{"type":"text","value":" deleted the context before notifying a listener snapshot; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear()"},{"type":"text","value":" returned an unsubscribe callback ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.ts:171-183"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retire "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":" clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit rejection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nested publications shared a context. Recorded listener failure preceded later graph failure; clearing could not replace the primary error ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.ts:188-245"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failure-identity clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compiler's pipeline received its output operator before finalization and was cleared with graph/input references on disposal ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:386-389,467-503,1096-1101"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One-use field clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tracksPublishedRows"},{"type":"text","value":" was set before the ordered loader started and selected callback-visible membership classification rather than immediate delta classification ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:571-664,948-968,1156-1197"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Duplicate-state clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit rejection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordered repair held callback delivery across participants and could transfer that hold to truncate replay. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"publishedRows"},{"type":"text","value":" retained the prior visible values ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:409-428,819-861,924-968"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field-removal clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source live-query builders became graph dependencies during subscription and were passed to the shared scheduler ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:548-553,803-817"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queued-only clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contextId"},{"type":"text","value":" remained a live override beside the unused job ID and dependency overrides. The queued callback was fenced by sync-run generation ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:651-691"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Window moves, demand settlement, ordered-load completion, initial sync, and source recovery each scheduled graph work ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:336-339,406-416,491-528,762-766,1091-1105"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Low salience"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Even an initially empty graph turn checked loaders, processed synchronous writes through D2, flushed, then evaluated readiness ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:571-645"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queue clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordered-load settlement checked sync-run identity before changing failure state. Its final success scheduled a publication run ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:491-528"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recovery clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The dependency matrix crossed source order, pending-aware state, and requeue. It required the dependent to see the final source run ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:132-179"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synthetic-test replacement clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The clear-listener test checked listener snapshot mutation, multiple failures, first-error retention, and the next clear ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:280-313"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retire "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear"},{"type":"text","value":" clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit rejection"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Publication tests checked nested timing, discarded jobs, first-error precedence, thrown "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":", later delivery, and coherent dependent state ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:182-278,579-727"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failure-identity clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collection/Effect cases crossed shared and derived sources plus write order; diamond and hybrid joins required one coherent dependent run ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:1059-1367"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synthetic-test replacement clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restart cases separated obsolete resolve/reject from replacement state; loader cases checked writes during graph turns ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:1443-1631"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recovery clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Repeated lexical aliases attempted every loader and kept the exact first falsy failure ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:1633-1771"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failure-identity clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rescheduling replaces a callback while retaining queue position; omission of new dependencies retains the old set ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.ts:70-94"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queued-only clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A running prerequisite leaves the map before its callback; requeueing it blocks its dependent. A no-progress pass throws ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.ts:98-145"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queued-only clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nested publications share the outer context. Graph work flushes afterward; the first listener error has precedence, and failure clears jobs/context ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.ts:173-226"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failure/recovery clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compiler closures retain mutable subscriptions. Startup buffers changes until subscriptions exist, drains them to D2, then runs the graph ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:389,519-750"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One-use pipeline clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ordered-loader map supplies the tracking condition; the separate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"publishedRows"},{"type":"text","value":" map retains callback-visible membership and values ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:405,939-959,1150"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Duplicate-state clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After Effect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordered repair and inherited replay holds still gate callbacks across participants. Final success flushes; failure keeps private deltas hidden ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"effect.ts:814-861"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Field-removal clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Low salience"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"contextId"},{"type":"text","value":", builder dependencies, and sync-run fencing remain in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduleGraphRun"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:651-685"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Override clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Empty-start graph turns still check loaders and process synchronous writes before publication ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:571-645"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queue clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordered-load settlement is sync-run-fenced. Window failures, replay, ordered loads, and joined demand still gate publication ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:491-528,908-936"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recovery clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After builder"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Child facades prepare before root commit; failure discards them, while root and facade notifications follow state installation ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-config-builder.ts:930-981"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scheduler-focused reduction"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Low salience"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source/dependent order and prerequisite requeue form a four-case matrix that checks the final source run ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:132-165"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancellation clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listener snapshot, first-error, later delivery, and falsy-failure matrices remain in public publication-path tests ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:388-727"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failure/recovery clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Collection/Effect, shared/derived, write-order, diamond, and hybrid cases check coherent dependent publication ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:1035-1367"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Synthetic-test replacement clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Category mismatch"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After scheduler test"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restart and repeated-alias cases retain stale-settlement and exact first-failure distinctions ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scheduler.test.ts:1419-1771"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recovery clause"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compression"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The before-only scan cannot establish repository-wide caller absence. The separate repository search found no production call to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onClear()"},{"type":"text","value":" or implementation of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasPendingGraphRun()"},{"type":"text","value":" at the code target. The after-only scan found no explicit rejection in the frozen summary. Each scan returned its own source pointers before collation."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"pr-1909-code-weight-loss-audit","text":"PR #1909 code-weight loss audit","level":1}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# PR #1909 code-weight loss audit\n\nFrozen reduction: Retire internal `Scheduler.onClear` notifications and pending-aware dependency objects because production has no callers. Dependencies then wait only for queued jobs. Replace synthetic tests with queued-job cancellation, exact failure identity, and recovery checks. Remove Effect's retained `pipeline` and `tracksPublishedRows` fields because the first is used once and the second duplicates the ordered-loader map. Remove unused `scheduleGraphRun` job ID and dependency overrides.\n\nThe before source is commit `80421c8b`. The after source is code commit `b69c189c`. Two agents scanned the source versions separately after reading the field-lab loss-audit card and live-query architecture. The entries below are source-supported omissions from the frozen reduction. They do not decide whether to restore an item or whether a behavior regressed.\n\n| Source | Recovered distinction and pointer | Where dropped | Rule |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Before scheduler | A dependency could block through `hasPendingGraphRun(contextId)` even without a queued job. Otherwise an absent dependency was satisfied (`80421c8b:scheduler.ts:126-144`). | Queued-only clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before scheduler | Rescheduling replaced a callback without moving its queue position; omitted dependencies retained the prior set. A running job left the map before reentrant work (`scheduler.ts:84-101,147-152`). | Cancellation clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler | `clear()` deleted the context before notifying a listener snapshot; `onClear()` returned an unsubscribe callback (`scheduler.ts:171-183`). | Retire `onClear` clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before scheduler | Nested publications shared a context. Recorded listener failure preceded later graph failure; clearing could not replace the primary error (`scheduler.ts:188-245`). | Failure-identity clause | Compression |\n| Before Effect | The compiler's pipeline received its output operator before finalization and was cleared with graph/input references on disposal (`effect.ts:386-389,467-503,1096-1101`). | One-use field clause | Compression |\n| Before Effect | `tracksPublishedRows` was set before the ordered loader started and selected callback-visible membership classification rather than immediate delta classification (`effect.ts:571-664,948-968,1156-1197`). | Duplicate-state clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before Effect | Ordered repair held callback delivery across participants and could transfer that hold to truncate replay. `publishedRows` retained the prior visible values (`effect.ts:409-428,819-861,924-968`). | Field-removal clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before Effect | Source live-query builders became graph dependencies during subscription and were passed to the shared scheduler (`effect.ts:548-553,803-817`). | Queued-only clause | Compression |\n| Before builder | `contextId` remained a live override beside the unused job ID and dependency overrides. The queued callback was fenced by sync-run generation (`collection-config-builder.ts:651-691`). | Override clause | Compression |\n| Before builder | Window moves, demand settlement, ordered-load completion, initial sync, and source recovery each scheduled graph work (`collection-config-builder.ts:336-339,406-416,491-528,762-766,1091-1105`). | Override clause | Low salience |\n| Before builder | Even an initially empty graph turn checked loaders, processed synchronous writes through D2, flushed, then evaluated readiness (`collection-config-builder.ts:571-645`). | Queue clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before builder | Ordered-load settlement checked sync-run identity before changing failure state. Its final success scheduled a publication run (`collection-config-builder.ts:491-528`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler test | The dependency matrix crossed source order, pending-aware state, and requeue. It required the dependent to see the final source run (`scheduler.test.ts:132-179`). | Synthetic-test replacement clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before scheduler test | The clear-listener test checked listener snapshot mutation, multiple failures, first-error retention, and the next clear (`scheduler.test.ts:280-313`). | Retire `onClear` clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before scheduler test | Publication tests checked nested timing, discarded jobs, first-error precedence, thrown `undefined`, later delivery, and coherent dependent state (`scheduler.test.ts:182-278,579-727`). | Failure-identity clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler test | Collection/Effect cases crossed shared and derived sources plus write order; diamond and hybrid joins required one coherent dependent run (`scheduler.test.ts:1059-1367`). | Synthetic-test replacement clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before scheduler test | Restart cases separated obsolete resolve/reject from replacement state; loader cases checked writes during graph turns (`scheduler.test.ts:1443-1631`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler test | Repeated lexical aliases attempted every loader and kept the exact first falsy failure (`scheduler.test.ts:1633-1771`). | Failure-identity clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler | Rescheduling replaces a callback while retaining queue position; omission of new dependencies retains the old set (`scheduler.ts:70-94`). | Queued-only clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler | A running prerequisite leaves the map before its callback; requeueing it blocks its dependent. A no-progress pass throws (`scheduler.ts:98-145`). | Queued-only clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler | Nested publications share the outer context. Graph work flushes afterward; the first listener error has precedence, and failure clears jobs/context (`scheduler.ts:173-226`). | Failure/recovery clause | Compression |\n| After Effect | Compiler closures retain mutable subscriptions. Startup buffers changes until subscriptions exist, drains them to D2, then runs the graph (`effect.ts:389,519-750`). | One-use pipeline clause | Category mismatch |\n| After Effect | The ordered-loader map supplies the tracking condition; the separate `publishedRows` map retains callback-visible membership and values (`effect.ts:405,939-959,1150`). | Duplicate-state clause | Compression |\n| After Effect | Ordered repair and inherited replay holds still gate callbacks across participants. Final success flushes; failure keeps private deltas hidden (`effect.ts:814-861`). | Field-removal clause | Low salience |\n| After builder | `contextId`, builder dependencies, and sync-run fencing remain in `scheduleGraphRun` (`collection-config-builder.ts:651-685`). | Override clause | Compression |\n| After builder | Empty-start graph turns still check loaders and process synchronous writes before publication (`collection-config-builder.ts:571-645`). | Queue clause | Category mismatch |\n| After builder | Ordered-load settlement is sync-run-fenced. Window failures, replay, ordered loads, and joined demand still gate publication (`collection-config-builder.ts:491-528,908-936`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n| After builder | Child facades prepare before root commit; failure discards them, while root and facade notifications follow state installation (`collection-config-builder.ts:930-981`). | Scheduler-focused reduction | Low salience |\n| After scheduler test | Source/dependent order and prerequisite requeue form a four-case matrix that checks the final source run (`scheduler.test.ts:132-165`). | Cancellation clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler test | Listener snapshot, first-error, later delivery, and falsy-failure matrices remain in public publication-path tests (`scheduler.test.ts:388-727`). | Failure/recovery clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler test | Collection/Effect, shared/derived, write-order, diamond, and hybrid cases check coherent dependent publication (`scheduler.test.ts:1035-1367`). | Synthetic-test replacement clause | Category mismatch |\n| After scheduler test | Restart and repeated-alias cases retain stale-settlement and exact first-failure distinctions (`scheduler.test.ts:1419-1771`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n\nThe before-only scan cannot establish repository-wide caller absence. The separate repository search found no production call to `onClear()` or implementation of `hasPendingGraphRun()` at the code target. The after-only scan found no explicit rejection in the frozen summary. Each scan returned its own source pointers before collation.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# PR #1909 code-weight loss audit\n\nFrozen reduction: Retire internal `Scheduler.onClear` notifications and pending-aware dependency objects because production has no callers. Dependencies then wait only for queued jobs. Replace synthetic tests with queued-job cancellation, exact failure identity, and recovery checks. Remove Effect's retained `pipeline` and `tracksPublishedRows` fields because the first is used once and the second duplicates the ordered-loader map. Remove unused `scheduleGraphRun` job ID and dependency overrides.\n\nThe before source is commit `80421c8b`. The after source is code commit `b69c189c`. Two agents scanned the source versions separately after reading the field-lab loss-audit card and live-query architecture. The entries below are source-supported omissions from the frozen reduction. They do not decide whether to restore an item or whether a behavior regressed.\n\n| Source | Recovered distinction and pointer | Where dropped | Rule |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Before scheduler | A dependency could block through `hasPendingGraphRun(contextId)` even without a queued job. Otherwise an absent dependency was satisfied (`80421c8b:scheduler.ts:126-144`). | Queued-only clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before scheduler | Rescheduling replaced a callback without moving its queue position; omitted dependencies retained the prior set. A running job left the map before reentrant work (`scheduler.ts:84-101,147-152`). | Cancellation clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler | `clear()` deleted the context before notifying a listener snapshot; `onClear()` returned an unsubscribe callback (`scheduler.ts:171-183`). | Retire `onClear` clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before scheduler | Nested publications shared a context. Recorded listener failure preceded later graph failure; clearing could not replace the primary error (`scheduler.ts:188-245`). | Failure-identity clause | Compression |\n| Before Effect | The compiler's pipeline received its output operator before finalization and was cleared with graph/input references on disposal (`effect.ts:386-389,467-503,1096-1101`). | One-use field clause | Compression |\n| Before Effect | `tracksPublishedRows` was set before the ordered loader started and selected callback-visible membership classification rather than immediate delta classification (`effect.ts:571-664,948-968,1156-1197`). | Duplicate-state clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before Effect | Ordered repair held callback delivery across participants and could transfer that hold to truncate replay. `publishedRows` retained the prior visible values (`effect.ts:409-428,819-861,924-968`). | Field-removal clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before Effect | Source live-query builders became graph dependencies during subscription and were passed to the shared scheduler (`effect.ts:548-553,803-817`). | Queued-only clause | Compression |\n| Before builder | `contextId` remained a live override beside the unused job ID and dependency overrides. The queued callback was fenced by sync-run generation (`collection-config-builder.ts:651-691`). | Override clause | Compression |\n| Before builder | Window moves, demand settlement, ordered-load completion, initial sync, and source recovery each scheduled graph work (`collection-config-builder.ts:336-339,406-416,491-528,762-766,1091-1105`). | Override clause | Low salience |\n| Before builder | Even an initially empty graph turn checked loaders, processed synchronous writes through D2, flushed, then evaluated readiness (`collection-config-builder.ts:571-645`). | Queue clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before builder | Ordered-load settlement checked sync-run identity before changing failure state. Its final success scheduled a publication run (`collection-config-builder.ts:491-528`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler test | The dependency matrix crossed source order, pending-aware state, and requeue. It required the dependent to see the final source run (`scheduler.test.ts:132-179`). | Synthetic-test replacement clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before scheduler test | The clear-listener test checked listener snapshot mutation, multiple failures, first-error retention, and the next clear (`scheduler.test.ts:280-313`). | Retire `onClear` clause | Explicit rejection |\n| Before scheduler test | Publication tests checked nested timing, discarded jobs, first-error precedence, thrown `undefined`, later delivery, and coherent dependent state (`scheduler.test.ts:182-278,579-727`). | Failure-identity clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler test | Collection/Effect cases crossed shared and derived sources plus write order; diamond and hybrid joins required one coherent dependent run (`scheduler.test.ts:1059-1367`). | Synthetic-test replacement clause | Category mismatch |\n| Before scheduler test | Restart cases separated obsolete resolve/reject from replacement state; loader cases checked writes during graph turns (`scheduler.test.ts:1443-1631`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n| Before scheduler test | Repeated lexical aliases attempted every loader and kept the exact first falsy failure (`scheduler.test.ts:1633-1771`). | Failure-identity clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler | Rescheduling replaces a callback while retaining queue position; omission of new dependencies retains the old set (`scheduler.ts:70-94`). | Queued-only clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler | A running prerequisite leaves the map before its callback; requeueing it blocks its dependent. A no-progress pass throws (`scheduler.ts:98-145`). | Queued-only clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler | Nested publications share the outer context. Graph work flushes afterward; the first listener error has precedence, and failure clears jobs/context (`scheduler.ts:173-226`). | Failure/recovery clause | Compression |\n| After Effect | Compiler closures retain mutable subscriptions. Startup buffers changes until subscriptions exist, drains them to D2, then runs the graph (`effect.ts:389,519-750`). | One-use pipeline clause | Category mismatch |\n| After Effect | The ordered-loader map supplies the tracking condition; the separate `publishedRows` map retains callback-visible membership and values (`effect.ts:405,939-959,1150`). | Duplicate-state clause | Compression |\n| After Effect | Ordered repair and inherited replay holds still gate callbacks across participants. Final success flushes; failure keeps private deltas hidden (`effect.ts:814-861`). | Field-removal clause | Low salience |\n| After builder | `contextId`, builder dependencies, and sync-run fencing remain in `scheduleGraphRun` (`collection-config-builder.ts:651-685`). | Override clause | Compression |\n| After builder | Empty-start graph turns still check loaders and process synchronous writes before publication (`collection-config-builder.ts:571-645`). | Queue clause | Category mismatch |\n| After builder | Ordered-load settlement is sync-run-fenced. Window failures, replay, ordered loads, and joined demand still gate publication (`collection-config-builder.ts:491-528,908-936`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n| After builder | Child facades prepare before root commit; failure discards them, while root and facade notifications follow state installation (`collection-config-builder.ts:930-981`). | Scheduler-focused reduction | Low salience |\n| After scheduler test | Source/dependent order and prerequisite requeue form a four-case matrix that checks the final source run (`scheduler.test.ts:132-165`). | Cancellation clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler test | Listener snapshot, first-error, later delivery, and falsy-failure matrices remain in public publication-path tests (`scheduler.test.ts:388-727`). | Failure/recovery clause | Compression |\n| After scheduler test | Collection/Effect, shared/derived, write-order, diamond, and hybrid cases check coherent dependent publication (`scheduler.test.ts:1035-1367`). | Synthetic-test replacement clause | Category mismatch |\n| After scheduler test | Restart and repeated-alias cases retain stale-settlement and exact first-failure distinctions (`scheduler.test.ts:1419-1771`). | Recovery clause | Compression |\n\nThe before-only scan cannot establish repository-wide caller absence. The separate repository search found no production call to `onClear()` or implementation of `hasPendingGraphRun()` at the code target. The after-only scan found no explicit rejection in the frozen summary. Each scan returned its own source pointers before collation.\n"}
